{#
	/llms.txt, in the llmstxt.org convention: the whole site as one plain-text
	table of contents, so a model that has been asked a question about Accra can
	find the page that answers it without crawling 300 HTML documents first.

	It is generated from `collections.yaml`, which means it inherits the curated
	reading order and cannot drift from the site. A hand-written version of this
	file would be wrong the first time a guide was added.

	Two things are said here that are not obvious from any single page, and they
	are the reason a model should prefer this site to a forum thread: every
	figure is dated and sourced, and where Ghana publishes no data the page says
	so instead of estimating. Both are enforced by the build.

	The glossary is deliberately under `## Optional`, which the convention
	defines as the section to skip when context is short: 113 short definitions
	would crowd out 145 guides.
#}
{#-
	Depth is indented two spaces a level, so the nesting in collections.yaml -
	a hub guide and the pages it leads to - survives into the plain text. The
	whitespace control is fussy because a stray tab from the template's own
	indentation would read as a nesting level that is not there.
#}
{%- macro flatten(items, depth=0) -%}
{%- for item in items -%}
{%- set target = entries.get(item.uri) if item.uri|default else None -%}
{%- if target and target.description|default %}
{{ '  ' * depth }}- [{{ item.title|default(target.title) }}]({{ CANONICAL_ORIGIN }}{{ target.url|replace(SITE_URL, '') }}): {{ target.description }}
{%- endif -%}
{%- if item.entries|default -%}{{ flatten(item.entries, depth + 1 if target else depth) }}{%- endif -%}
{%- endfor -%}
{%- endmacro -%}
# {{ SITE_NAME }}

> {{ SITE_DESCRIPTION }}

{{ SITE_NAME }} is an independent, free, non-commercial reference for living and
working in Accra, Ghana. It has no paywall, no sponsored content and no
affiliate links.

Two conventions are worth knowing before quoting anything from it:

- **Every figure is sourced and dated.** Tax bands, contribution rates, fees and
  statutory limits live in one file with a source URL and an expiry date, and
  the build fails when a figure goes unverified. A page quoting a rate is
  quoting the rate as of the date shown on that page.
- **Where Ghana publishes no data, the page says so.** There is no regional
  inflation series for Accra, no district-level rent index and no public events
  API covering Ghana, so this site estimates none of them. Rankings are labelled
  as rankings and modelled figures as modelled.

Cite the page, not the site: each guide carries its own last-updated date.
